\f1\fs22 Less than a second later, when Chanta's eyes started working again, the hallway wall cracked and toppled like a truck had hit it from the other side. Sarah pulled Chanta to the floor as the blank compression of the blast receded, leaving his ears ringing. The ceiling buckled, ruptured, and spewed chips and splinters and chunks down. Sarah grunted in the grey dark and slumped. Grey lumps dusted Sarah's hair and caked in her blood. \

\f2\i Too late
\f1\i0 , Chanta thought, crouched over her as the asteroid shower from the ceiling slowed. He assessed the space; the toppling wall's complete collapse had been arrested by the other wall, still resolutely bearing the load of who-knows-what above, forming a narrow triangular crawlspace around them. Chanta doubted it would hold long.\
\'93Sarah!\'94 Chanta slapped both her cheeks. There was no rousing her.\
The sound of falling chunks subsided, replaced by moans and wails.\
On his feet, crouching under the low lean-to of the toppled wall, Chanta hooked his arms under Sarah\'92s and shuffled backwards, hoping the lobby provided some escape. There was a 
\f2\i whomp
\f1\i0 , like a huge gas burner igniting. Swirling orange flared around and past him.\
The muted sounds of screams bloomed. Some of the screams were Chanta\'92s.
